  "name": "Nightscout",
  "alternateName": [
    "cgm-remote-monitor"
  ],
  "description": "Web platform for real-time continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) data broadcasting, storage, and visualisation. Acts as a personal diabetes data hub ingesting CGM readings from Dexcom, FreeStyle Libre, Medtronic, and other sources, storing data in MongoDB, and serving a browser dashboard, REST API, and GraphQL endpoint for caregivers, clinicians, and AID systems. Supports configurable glucose alarms, treatment logging, AGP reports, and integration with Loop, AndroidAPS, and Trio. Deployable to free-tier cloud platforms or self-hosted Docker. AGPL-3.0, 2.8k stars with 73k forks reflecting extraordinary real-world DIY deployment, v15.0.7 (April 2026). The de facto remote monitoring platform of the #WeAreNotWaiting diabetes community since 2013.",
